What about the commit callback in cache.js storing even if... commit only called when flight still registered per fix. But also consider: flight A registered; invalidate → forget; get → flight B registered; B resolves first, commits, deletes itself, stores value with deadline; then A resolves — pending.get(key) is undefined ≠ A → no commit. ✓ matches visible test.

Reverse: A resolves first after invalidate+flight B started? A detached → no commit, no delete. B still pending. ✓

